  "notes": "Elevated TNL Ratio Period: after a Permitted Acquisition, or series of them, with consideration over $25M, the Borrowers may raise the total net leverage maximum from 4.00x to 4.50x. The higher level applies for the acquisition quarter and the next three quarters. Only one such period may run at a time, and at least one quarter at 4.00x must separate two periods. The 4.00x level is quoted as written ('4:00 to 1.00'). Financial covenants are calculated excluding the assets, liabilities and operations of Excluded Subsidiaries, except liabilities of Excluded Subsidiaries that are recourse to the Borrowers. Excluded Interim Debt (refinanced debt whose proceeds are held in a pledged blocked account) is excluded from Consolidated Funded Debt for covenant purposes. Netted cash is unencumbered cash and Cash Equivalents of the Parent and its Domestic Subsidiaries, capped at $100M. EBITDA add-backs: non-cash asset sale losses and impairment, abandonment or closure charges are capped at $50M cumulative from closing. Cash and non-cash severance and reorganization charges are capped at $10M cumulative. Other add-backs include acquisition expenses and integration costs, financing and disposition fees, derivative charges, PIK dividend charges, IRB write-offs, and other non-cash items acceptable to the Agent. Pro forma acquired-business EBITDA may include expected synergies up to 15% of Consolidated EBITDA, or another amount agreed with the Agent. Non-recurring private-company expenses may be added back, but not for the interest coverage test. Limited Condition Acquisition provisions do not apply pro forma treatment to Section 7.11 compliance until the acquisition closes. Financial covenant amendments require only Required Lenders. Incremental facilities may carry different or no financial covenants, but only if no more restrictive. Section 7.03(j) debt cannot carry a financial maintenance covenant unless it is also added for the Revolving Credit Lenders. Pricing grid is based on Consolidated Total Net Leverage Ratio, with sustainability-linked (KPI) margin adjustments through FY2026. The facility is secured. Each subsidiary is a co-Borrower jointly and severally liable rather than a guarantor.",
  "terms": [
