      "section": "Section 10.01(i)",
      "quote": "(i) subordinate the right of payment of the Obligations hereunder to any other Indebtedness or other obligation or (ii) subordinate the Liens on a material portion of the Collateral securing the Obligations to Liens securing any other Indebtedness or other obligation without the written consent of each Lender directly and adversely affected thereby",
      "summary": "Payment subordination of the Obligations, or lien subordination on a material portion of the Collateral, requires consent of each directly and adversely affected lender. Exceptions are subordination permitted under Section 9.10 as in effect at closing, such as purchase-money liens under 7.01(a). There is no express language addressing non-pro-rata exchanges or open-market purchases.",
      "quote_verified": true
    },
    {
